														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4476211">
									

<p>I guess what I was trying to do was keep the article more concise. Instead of building a mystery, I was trying to lean more into the horror of the idea of being trapped in a piece of your own body, most of which I tried to develop in the Addendum. I see what you're saying about the testing logs - they are the first non-description piece you really get to - but maybe they could actually be removed, allowing the reader a quicker transition into the rest of the addendum?</p>
<p>As for your second point (the redacted addendum) the reason I did that was because I felt it would work better to let the reader's mind fill in the blank rather than just say &quot;he was left as a pile of animate bowels.&quot;</p>
<p>Also, yeah, i had a bit of trouble with the penultimate addendum. But it's not meant to be a standalone addendum as much as it's meant to tie in with the final one - if you look at it, it essentially means that, despite the horrific state the first batch of -1s were recovered in, they actually wouldn't be eligible for euthanization since they are technically capable of rudimentary communication.</p>

							</div>

								
